Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(web): give every authenticated browser Host settings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Resolve settings persistence from the browser session instead of the page
authority. The dist root and `/api` share one browser-session check, so a page
that loaded — loopback or LAN-paired — already authenticated to this Host.
Selecting memory mode off-loopback left the Models page failing with
"settings are unavailable in this browser", the Plugins section with no
configurable namespace, and theme, locale, and onboarding preferences
process-local.

`ui-settings` now resolves `host` unconditionally. The memory mode stays the
mechanism's other value for a composition that wants process-local
preferences, and `isLoopback` keeps gating the native Host document action in
ui-settings-general.

The apply specs of ui-settings, ui-theme, ui-settings-general, and
ui-settings-models pin the new composition, the remote-welcome web e2e now
asserts the acknowledgement reaches the durable document and survives a
reload, and the Agent Note records the superseded locality rule.
